# Nonprofit Roadmap batch pull requests

Each **batch PR** (up to five top-level task codes, e.g. 2.1–2.5) is the **implementation ticket**. Work happens on **that PR and branch**, not on follow-up PRs per task.

## Do

- Branch prefix: `cursor/nonprofit/` (e.g. `cursor/nonprofit/s02-b1-340a`).
- Title: `NPO S{n} B{n} {section title} ({task range})` — **never** put "stub" in the title or body.
- Read task specs from the catalog (`nonprofit-catalog.ts`) or generate a fresh body: `pnpm npo:batch-pr-body --pr <number>`.
- Implement **every task in the batch** on the same branch; use Who / What / Where / Why / When / How and **Done when** from the catalog.
- Merge with green CI to mark those task codes complete on the Nonprofit Roadmap board.

## GitHub: block merge until the right checks pass

On **main**, use branch protection so merges wait on CI:

- **Require before merge (on the PR):** workflow **Tests and Vercel deploy** → job **Playwright E2E** (GitHub may show `(pull_request)` on PR runs).
- **After merge on main:** the same workflow runs on **push**; **Deploy to Vercel (production)** only runs there. Roadmap task completion also needs **Playwright E2E (push)** and **Deploy to Vercel (production)** green on the **merge commit SHA** (see `src/lib/roadmap/required-checks.ts`).
- **Do not merge** an NPO batch PR while **Tests and Vercel deploy / Playwright E2E** is red on that PR.

Optional: require the production deploy check only if you gate merges on post-merge push runs; you can still require Playwright on the PR and treat a red post-merge deploy as a fix-on-branch problem below.

## Deploy failure / same PR only

If **Playwright** or **production deploy** fails on a batch PR or on **main** right after that batch merged:

- **Fix on the same batch branch and PR** — push commits to `cursor/nonprofit/s…-b…-340a`, re-run CI, then merge (or merge again after revert if already on main).
- **Do not** open a unrelated “deploy fix” PR for batch scope; that does not re-run completion on the batch merge SHA agents expect.
- After merge, if tasks stay **locked** because push deploy was cancelled or red, re-run **Tests and Vercel deploy** on the merge SHA or use workflow_dispatch **roadmap_backfill_pr** + **roadmap_backfill_sha** in `.github/workflows/run-tests.yml` (see roadmap webhook backfill).

## Do not

- Do **not** treat batch PRs as placeholders that forbid product code.
- Do **not** open separate PRs per task code (`NPO 2.1 …`, `cursor/nonprofit/2-2.1-slug`, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks for an exception.
- Do **not** copy legacy "catalog stub only" or "merging does not mark tasks complete" text into new PR descriptions (that was wrong for most batches).

## Exception: Section 1 batch 1

- PR **#109** is a **board placeholder only** (merge completes nothing).
- Implement tasks **1.1–1.5** on PR **#131** (same batch scope).

## New sidebar pages (auth)

App pages under `src/app/(root)/` are **protected by default** (`src/lib/auth/protectedRoutes.ts`). You do **not** need a PR one-liner to register each path — only add a **public** prefix if the route is intentionally unauthenticated (marketing, `/negotiate/[token]`, etc.).

Edge proxy and AuthContext share the same rule via `isProtectedAppRoute` / `isProxyProtectedPath`.

